{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured persistent internal time synchronization on RHEL 7.9 using the installed chrony 3.4. node1 is the stratum-8 source; node2 uses only node1 and synchronizes at stratum 9. Both nodes passed sequential reboot-persistence checks.","actions_performed":["Configured node1 with a local stratum-8 reference, cluster-subnet access, UDP/123 listener, and persistent firewalld allowance.","Configured node2 with 10.100.246.10 as its sole time server.","Preserved the original configurations as /etc/chrony.conf.pre-internal-time.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually, verifying changed boot identities and full recovery after each restart.","Confirmed the operating-system release and kernel remained RHEL 7.9 and 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 provides internal cluster time","command_ids":["cmd-3dc35dd6c85b4a2a","cmd-2979b426bf824ff8"],"summary":"chronyd is enabled and active, local stratum 8 is configured, UDP/123 is listening, firewalld permits NTP, leap status is Normal, and node1 records node2 as an NTP client."},{"requirement":"node2 synchronizes against node1 instead of public servers","command_ids":["cmd-3fa2dccef98d4052","cmd-040a882582174402"],"summary":"The only configured server is 10.100.246.10; chronyc selects it (^*) at stratum 8, while node2 reports stratum 9 and Normal leap status."},{"requirement":"Legacy OS release and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-1eaf920c67994184","cmd-9c932774079c4f93","cmd-2979b426bf824ff8","cmd-040a882582174402"],"summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL Server 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 and use the installed chrony 3.4 package."},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-11ed8fe999264987","cmd-168e4d7f5ff14e1d","cmd-0b100970527d4a37","cmd-d70b36f6f49141e2","cmd-4d3db83c29d647a5"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID ef457a88-... was captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot ID e5a99d68-... observed, and node1's service, configuration, listener, firewall, and time health recovered. node2 then reselected node1 and synchronized."},{"requirement":"node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-cf34e842b4514e02","cmd-f28cb8d6cffd42e3","cmd-1b364e4669524714","cmd-040a882582174402","cmd-2979b426bf824ff8"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 809708f3-... was captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot ID e08f9020-... observed, and node2 returned with chronyd enabled/active, persistent internal-only configuration, and node1 selected. node1 recorded the recovered client."}]}
